{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"My dearest Marie,\n\nI am back in my room, exhausted but content. This morning I spent two hours in the Esterhazy gallery, a third visit, but I confess the private cabinet dazzled me. The valet was courteous, though perhaps too eager to point out every crack in the plaster. I saw the Rubens, which is indeed magnificent, but the lighting here is dim; I paid two florins for the privilege of seeing it poorly.\n\nLunch was with Sonnleitner and a Paduan professor. The wine was good, the roast pheasant excellent, and the conversation light. Sonnleitner is a solid man, if a bit dull on the subject of Roman law. We paid three guilders each, a fair sum for the heat.\n\nIn the evening I saw Rossini’s *Corradino*. The music is intoxicating, though the libretto drags in the second act. I nearly dozed off during the recitatives, but the chorus woke me. It is a spectacle, not a thought.\n\nYou asked about the snuff; I bought a tin of the finest brand here. It is strong. I miss your quiet, and the boys’ noise. I shall write more soon.\n\nYours,\nG.W.F."}}],"created":1795219347,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":263,"prompt_tokens":1126,"total_tokens":1389,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-DoprHWwTIvOwGocCHa26e5hAFCrPGNKO","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":1126,"prompt_ms":1053.386,"prompt_per_token_ms":0.9355115452930728,"prompt_per_second":1068.9338950773981,"predicted_n":263,"predicted_ms":6172.96,"predicted_per_token_ms":23.56091603053435,"predicted_per_second":42.443171509292135}}